a`, capacity/length untouched, no realloc | `err_02_arrgrowf_no_growth_returns_same` |\n| 3 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `elemsize == 0` (degenerate element size) | still allocates `0*min_cap + sizeof(header)`, `capacity = min_cap`, `length = 0` | `err_03_arrgrowf_zero_elemsize` |\n| 4 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | huge `min_cap`/`addlen` so `elemsize*min_cap + sizeof(hdr)` overflows / `realloc` fails → **no null check** at line 297 | UB in C (write through `NULL+32`). *Not exercised* — documented as out of scope; both libs would fault identically. | n/a (documented) |\n| 5 | `stbds_arrfreef` | `a == NULL` → `free(stbds_header(NULL))` = `free((char*)0 - 32)` | UB/`free(): invalid pointer` abort. *Not exercised.* | n/a (documented) |\n| 6 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | `a == NULL` (line 573) | returns immediately, no free, no crash | `err_06_hmfree_null` |\n| 7 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | valid `a` whose `hash_table == NULL` (line 574) | skips the strdup sweep and `strreset`, still frees `hash_table` (NULL) and the header | `err_07_hmfree_no_table` |\n| 8 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` | probe reaches a bucket slot with `hash == STBDS_HASH_EMPTY (0)` (lines 609-611 / 620-622) | returns **`-1`** | covered via rows 10-12 |\n| 9 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `a == NULL` (line 634) | `*temp = STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY (-1)`; returns a **newly allocated** hash pointer (len 1, zeroed elem 0) | `err_09_hmget_ts_null_a` |\n| 10 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | valid `a` but `hash_table == 0` (line 644) — e.g. array built by `stbds_hmput_default` only | `*temp = -1`; returns `a` unchanged | `err_10_hmget_ts_no_table` |\n| 11 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | key not present in a populated table (`slot < 0`, line 648) | `*temp = STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY (-1)`; returns `a` unchanged | `err_11_hmget_ts_missing_key` |\n| 12 | `stbds_hmget_key` | any of rows 9-11 | same as `..._ts` plus `stbds_header(p-elemsize)->temp == -1` | `err_12_hmget_key_missing_writes_temp` |\n| 13 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a == NULL` (line 669) | allocates, `length = 1`, elem