"` fn aborts, so the two libraries fail with the same signal.\n`err_asserts_abort_parity` runs 7 scenarios (5 aborting, 2 clean) against each\nlibrary in a **subprocess** and asserts the termination statuses are identical.\nValidated with a negative control: a Rust `.so` rebuilt with the assert macro\nneutered makes that test fail, so it genuinely guards the behaviour.\n\nApart from that, `src/lib.rs` needed no changes. Every other fix during\nverification was to the *test harness*, where early versions read uninitialised\nC memory (`temp_key`, element padding), compared `malloc_usable_size` (not a\nfunction of the requested size), assumed `realloc` always moves the block, or\nexercised configurations on which the C itself faults.''')\ns=s.replace('''* **Totals** — 82 test functions''','''* **Asserts** — the C's 7 live `STBDS_ASSERT`s are reproduced; abort parity is\n  checked in subprocesses (`err_asserts_abort_parity`).\n* **Totals** — 85 test functions''')\ns=s.replace('''* **Phase C** — 42 of 44 `ERRORS.md` rows have a passing differential test; the''','''* **Phase C** — 42 of 44 `ERRORS.md` rows have a passing differential test; the''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ntimeout 600 ./verify.sh 2>&1 | grep -E '\\[ok\\] cargo test|\\[FAIL\\]|PASSED|FAILURES'","description":"Update VERIFICATION.md and run final full verification"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1501,"cache_read_input_tokens":351446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1501,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c378fbc5-cb29-4f2d-9c80-7b97c2b5be7b","uuid":"25922f29-b0bb-4eab-b3d8-7ae5aafa5de8","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:23:36.738Z"}
