{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_juh3pqsbjrekzl6qlqydradtyr4gr6lfphzo6gpihkvqp7go6xpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit complete. Note up front: `translation/src/lib.rs` was **edited by someone else while I was auditing** (asserts were added at 06:16–06:17). Everything below is against the current revision, md5 `81869781f08f1a22692ded4f9d56e491`, 1360 lines, mtime 2026-09-05 06:17:16. Both the debug and release `.so` on disk are built from that source.\n\n## Per-function verdict\n\n| # | Function | C lines | Rust lines | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | 631–657 | 744–779 | Exactly equivalent |\n| 2 | `stbds_hmget_key` | 659–665 | 782–795 | Exactly equivalent |\n| 3 | `stbds_hmput_default` | 667–676 | 802–818 | Exactly equivalent |\n| 4 | `stbds_hmput_key` | 680–794 | 825–1015 | Exactly equivalent (statement-for-statement, incl. the omitted `stbds_temp_key` in the wrap-around loop, the C 773–783 order/signedness, and the `switch` `default:` arm) |\n| 5 | `stbds_shmode_func` | 796–805 | 1022–1032 | Exactly equivalent (`mode as u8` == `(unsigned char) mode`) |\n| 6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | 807–868 | 1039–1139 | Equivalent except finding **D2** (unreachable) |\n| 7 | `stbds_strdup` | 870–876 | 1145–1151 | Exactly equivalent |\n| 8 | `stbds_stralloc` | 881–918 | 1158–1214 | Equivalent except finding **D1** (real, FFI-reachable) |\n| 9 | `stbds_strreset` | 920–930 | 1218–1234 | Exactly equivalent |\n| 10 | `strkey` | 938–943 | 1243–1281 | Exactly equivalent — byte-for-byte incl. the NUL and stale tail bytes |\n| 11 | `arr_del` / `arrpush_int` | 945–958 | 1289–1360 | Exactly equivalent (macro expansion + allocation sequence verified) |\n\nMacro helpers all check out: `stbds_header` (HDR_SIZE = 32 = `sizeof(stbds_array_header)`), `stbds_temp`, `stbds_temp_key` (writes through `header->hash_table`, i.e. `hash_index::temp_key`), `stbds_arrcap`/`stbds_arrlen` (both keep the `(a) ? … : 0` null guard and the `ptrdiff_t` cast), `STBDS_HASH_TO_ARR`/`STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH`, `stbds_hash_table`, and the `STBDS_SH_*` / `STBDS_HM_*` constants. `STBDS_OFFSETOF` has no Rust counterpart and needs none — it is only used by the C *header* macros (`hmdel`/`shdel`), which are not part of the `.so` ABI; `keyoffset` arrives as a parameter.\n\n**`mode` comparison sites — all 7 use the identical operator:** C 560→Rust 618 (`>=`), C 590→671 (`>=`), C 707→860 (`>=`), C 713→871 (`>=`), C 732→904 (`>=`), C 836→1091 (`==`), C 842→1104 (`==`). Signed `c_int` comparison in both, so negative / 2 / `INT_MAX` / `INT_MIN` all route identically.\n\n## Findings\n\n**D1 | `stbds_stralloc` | C 888 | Rust 1168 | REAL, confirmed empirically**\n- C: `blocksize = (size_t)512 << (a->block >> 1)`. `a->block` is `unsigned char`, so the shift count can be 0…127. For counts ≥ 64 this is UB, but gcc/x86-64 emits `shlq %cl` which masks the count to 6 bits, so e.g. `block == 128` → count `64 & 63 == 0` → `blocksize == 512`.\n- Rust: plain `<<`. With `overflow-checks = on` (the **dev** profile) a shift count ≥ 64 panics (`attempt to shift left with overflow`) → non-unwinding panic → `abort()`.\n- Distinguishing input: `stbds_string_arena a = {0}; a.block = 128; stbds_stralloc(&a, \"hello\");`\n  - C: returns a valid pointer, `a.block` becomes 129, `a.remaining == 506`, exit 0.\n  - Rust debug: SIGABRT (exit 134).\n  - Rust release (`overflow-checks = false`): matches C exactly.\n  - Also diverges for `block = 255`: C → `block` wraps to 0, `remaining == 0`, exit 0; Rust debug → abort.\n- Reachability: **not reachable through the library's own paths** — `stbds_hmput_key`'s `STBDS_SH_ARENA` arm saturates `block` at 22 (`512 << 11 == 2^20` is not `< 2^20`, so `++a->block` stops), giving a max shift count of 11. It *is* reachable by any external caller of the exported `stbds_stralloc`, which is how I triggered it. Fix: `STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MIN.wrapping_shl((blocksize >> 1) as u32)`.\n\n**D2 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | C 852 | Rust 1123 | theoretical only**\n- C: `stbds_header(raw_a)->length -= 1;` — `size_t`, wraps to `SIZE_MAX` if length were 0.\n- Rust: `(*stbds_header(raw_a)).length -= 1;` — plain `-=`, panics/aborts in the dev profile on underflow.\n- Distinguishing input: **not reachable via the public API.** Getting here needs `stbds_hm_find_slot` to return ≥ 0 while `header->length == 0`, i.e. a hash index holding an in-use entry for a zero-length array — no API sequence produces that. Only a caller that hand-edits `stbds_array_header::length` could. Cosmetically worth switching to `wrapping_sub(1)` for symmetry with the other counters.\n\n**D3 | all asserting functions | C 401/778/828/832/846/849/913 | Rust 352/978/1071/1082/1112/1117/1204 | cosmetic**\n- All seven C asserts are now present in Rust via `stbds_assert!` (`assert!`, not `debug_assert!`, so live in both profiles), at exactly the right point in the statement order (e.g. Rust 1071 fires *before* `used_count` is decremented, matching C 828 vs 829).\n- The only difference is the failure path's *appearance*: C prints `dt2: …/lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion 'slot >= 0' failed.` and `abort()`s directly; Rust prints a `panicked at src/lib.rs:1112` message plus `thread caused non-unwinding panic. aborting.` and then aborts. In the dev profile the Rust panic begins unwinding before hitting the `extern \"C\"` nounwind boundary — no `Drop` types exist in the crate, so nothing observable runs. Both terminate with SIGABRT / exit 134 at the same operation.\n\n## Verification evidence (differential harness, `translation/target/audit/`)\n\nBoth `.so`s `dlopen`'d with `RTLD_LOCAL` in one process; deterministic op traces (index returned, `temp_key`, every element, `length`, `capacity` after each op) diffed line-by-line, plus exit codes:\n\n- Binary hashmap, 40 000 mixed put/get/del ops × `mode ∈ {0, -1, INT_MIN}`: **80 000 lines identical** each.\n- String hashmap, 30 000 ops × `{SH_DEFAULT, SH_STRDUP, SH_ARENA} × mode ∈ {1, 2, 7, INT_MAX}`: identical, including the four `mode ≥ 2` runs where **both** libraries abort at the same op (78 identical lines, exit 134 in both) on the C-846 assert. This exercises the `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` vs `mode >= 1` mismatch you flagged — it is faithfully reproduced.\n- `shmode_func` mode truncation for `{0,1,2,3,4,255,256,257,258,-1,514,INT_MIN,INT_MAX}` plus 4 000-op runs at truncated modes `{256,257,258,259,260,511,-1}`: identical, including modes that truncate to the `default:` `memcpy` arm (and the resulting identical segfaults).\n- `stbds_stralloc`/`strreset`: 400 allocations mixing 1–4 000-byte and 60 000/150 000-byte strings — `remaining`, `block`, contents and reset state identical throughout (this covers `sizeof(*sb)-8+len`, both splice branches, and `p = storage + remaining - len`).\n- `strkey`: 22 values incl. `0, ±1, INT_MIN, INT_MAX, ±1e9`, compared as raw 32-byte hex dumps plus a long-then-short \"residue\" case — identical byte-for-byte.\n- `arr_del`: identical under a `realloc`/`free` LD_PRELOAD tracer — 8 × `realloc(NULL,48)`/`free` pairs, same order.\n- All of the above pass against **both** the debug and release Rust builds; the only debug-vs-release difference is D1."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1299,"cache_read_input_tokens":177735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1299,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01C59JXYoJuRXo48BLcttsvp","session_id":"c378fbc5-cb29-4f2d-9c80-7b97c2b5be7b","uuid":"a958ef29-7c29-45d8-93e9-b8d8b831eb2f","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:24:58.748Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit C vs Rust: map + arena + helpers"}
