ize >> 1);`\n   ->  use `wrapping_shl`, whose count is masked with `& 63` on a 64-bit target,\n   exactly like `shlq %cl`:\n   `blocksize = STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MIN.wrapping_shl((blocksize >> 1) as u32);`\n   Add a short comment saying gcc masks the shift count and that `a->block` can be\n   up to 255 because it is `unsigned char` and the function is exported.\n\n2. **`stbds_stralloc`, BOTH `stbds_realloc` calls** —\n   `core::mem::size_of::<stbds_string_block>() - 8 + len`\n   ->  `core::mem::size_of::<stbds_string_block>().wrapping_sub(8).wrapping_add(len)`\n   (and the same for the `+ blocksize` variant). Matches the C's `sizeof(*sb)-8+len`.\n\n3. **`stbds_hmdel_key`** — `(*stbds_header(raw_a)).length -= 1;`\n   ->  `(*stbds_header(raw_a)).length = (*stbds_header(raw_a)).length.wrapping_sub(1);`\n   (C line 852 is a `size_t` decrement that wraps.)\n\n4. **the three `(*stbds_header(a)).length += 1;`** in `stbds_hmget_key_ts`,\n   `stbds_hmput_default` and `stbds_hmput_key`\n   ->  `... = (...).length.wrapping_add(1);`\n\n5. **`stbds_hmput_key`**, in the `found_empty_slot` block:\n   - `(*stbds_header(a)).length = (i + 1) as usize;` -> `i.wrapping_add(1) as usize`\n   - `(*bucket).index[pos & STBDS_BUCKET_MASK] = i - 1;` -> `i.wrapping_sub(1)`\n   - `set_stbds_temp(a, i - 1);` -> `i.wrapping_sub(1)`\n   (`i` is `isize`, from `stbds_arrlen`.)\n\n6. **`stbds_hmdel_key`** — `let final_index: isize = stbds_arrlen(raw_a) - 1 - 1;`\n   ->  `stbds_arrlen(raw_a).wrapping_sub(1).wrapping_sub(1)`\n\n7. **`arrpush_int`** — `(*h).length = idx + 1;` -> `idx.wrapping_add(1)`\n\n## Do NOT change\n\n* the new `stbds_assert!` calls or the `stbds_assert!` macro — they are correct and\n  deliberately reproduce the C's live `assert`s. In particular\n  `(i as usize).wrapping_add(1) <= stbds_arrcap(a)` must stay as it is.\n* loop counters (`i += 1`, `j += 1`, `z += 1`, `n += 1` in `stbds_log2`,\n  `out += 1` / `nd += 1` / `nd -= 1` in `strkey`) — all provably bounded well below\